00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.309 align:start position:0%
colombians came out in mass to choose  the country's congressional lawmakers  and presidential candidates on sunday in  a vote that indicated a significant  political shift in this historically  conservative country  discontent in anger against traditional  parties and their neoliberal economic  policies boosted progressive and  independent candidates in the senate in  the house of representatives  we've had some rough times in the last  few years so i hope that this election  will bring some positive results and our  country will change  i think people are absolutely done tired  and worn out that the expectations as  citizens never materialized  unfortunately our old political class  has always played us  as leftist centrists and right-wing  coalitions tallied votes in their  respective primaries the night's clear  winner was gustavo petro a leftist  senator and former guerrilla who  received more than double the votes of  his closest rival right-wing candidate  federico gutierrez we saw a contraction  of the right wing  and a growth both from the centrist  parties and most significantly from the  left but what this means is that there  will be no single party or no single uh  political bloc with a majority in  congress for the next four years but it  also opens the possibility that a  leftist could win the presidency for the  first time in history something that has  right-wing voters on edge  i'm worried we need to defend democracy  on top of everything we can't allow a  leftist in power that's not convenient  for the country doesn't know how to  govern and is not transparent i fear  entrepreneurs will lose the ability to  hire people will not be able to afford a  home  fearing the possibility of fraud and  political violence more than 2 500  national and international observers  were deployed across the country  while voting was mostly peaceful two  soldiers died in bomb attacks in rural  areas where voters were called to choose  special representatives among victims of  the country's long civil conflict  what's clear is that this is a night to  remember for the supporters of gustavo  petra in his leftist coalition  an historic result that confirms that he  will be the candidate to beat in the  upcoming presidential elections in may  alessandro  al jazeera bogota
 

